[h1]UI Themes[/h1]

[h1]New colors for the game's interface: panels, buttons, tabs, lists and tooltips. Five themes included, switchable in game.[/h1]

[h2]/========== REQUIREMENTS ==========\[/h2]
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/lucky-wolf/DW2-Mod-Launcher/releases]DW2 Mod Launcher[/url] (recommended, to pick the theme in its settings)
[*]Tested with Distant Worlds 2 version 1.3.8.4
[/list]

[h2]/========== WHAT IT DOES ==========\[/h2]
[h3]Five themes[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Basalt[/b] (default)
[*][b]Amethyst[/b]
[*][b]Graphite[/b]
[*][b]Obsidian[/b]
[*][b]Synthwave[/b]
[/list]
Each theme recolors panel backgrounds, window headers, borders, buttons, active tabs, list selections, dropdowns, progress bars and the info boxes. Pick [b]Off[/b] to keep the game's own colors.

[h3]Cleaner panels and tooltips[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]No side gradient on panels:[/b] panel backgrounds are a single flat color, the selected object window included.
[*][b]Tooltips follow the theme:[/b] text tooltips and the tooltips of the selected object window use the theme's background.
[*][b]Solid tooltips:[/b] themes can draw tooltips without the panel's transparency, so the text behind them no longer shows through.
[/list]

[h3]Switch themes in game[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Ctrl+Alt+Plus[/b]: next theme (Off included). The theme name shows on screen.
[*][b]Ctrl+Alt+Minus[/b]: previous theme.
[*][b]Ctrl+Alt+0[/b]: shows the current theme.
[/list]
Buttons, tabs and list selections already on screen switch along with the theme. A theme switched this way lasts for the session; the theme in the launcher settings is the one used when the game starts.

[h2]/========== SETTINGS ==========\[/h2]
On the mod's settings page in the DW2 Mod Launcher:
[list]
[*][b]UI theme[/b] (Basalt by default): Off, Amethyst, Basalt, Graphite, Obsidian or Synthwave.
[/list]
Without the launcher, create [i]options.json[/i] in the mod's folder with [i]{"Theme": "Graphite"}[/i].

[h2]/========== MAKE YOUR OWN THEME ==========\[/h2]
Themes are plain JSON files in the mod's [i]themes[/i] folder. The easiest way to make one is the theme editor that comes with the mod:
[olist]
[*]Open [i]theme-editor.html[/i] from the mod's folder in your browser (it works offline).
[*]Start from one of the themes, adjust the colors on the preview and copy the JSON.
[*]Save it in the [i]themes[/i] folder as a new .json file.
[*]In game, press Ctrl+Alt+Plus until your theme shows up.
[/olist]
Colors are [i]#RRGGBB[/i], or [i]#RRGGBBAA[/i] to set transparency too. The folder is read again on every switch, so you can edit a theme with the game open and see it by switching away and back. To start the game with your own theme, put its name in [i]options.json[/i] (without the launcher).

[h2]/========== GOOD TO KNOW ==========\[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Works with the game's color schemes.[/b] The theme goes on top of the scheme chosen in the game's options. With Colorblind Assist, its warning and status colors stay in place.
[*][b]Not everything follows the theme.[/b] The system panel at the bottom center and map elements (selection frame, icons, population bar) keep the game's look.
[*][b]Log:[/b] data\Logs\DW2UIThemes\DW2UIThemes.log, in the game folder.
[/list]

[h2]/========== COMPATIBILITY ==========\[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Doesn't change any game data or saves.[/b] Colors are changed in memory only.
[*][b]Works in existing saves.[/b] Safe to add or remove at any time.
[*][b]Refreshed mods:[/b] tested together with the DW2 Refreshed series.
[*][b]Other UI mods:[/b] a mod that also changes interface colors may override some of the theme, or the other way around.
[/list]

[h2]/========== HOW TO USE THIS MOD ==========\[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Install the [url=https://github.com/lucky-wolf/DW2-Mod-Launcher/releases]DW2 Mod Launcher[/url] if you don't have it.
[*]Subscribe to this mod here in Steam Workshop.
[*]Start Distant Worlds 2 through the DW2 Mod Launcher, enable the mod and pick a theme in its settings.
[*]In game, try the other themes with Ctrl+Alt+Plus.
[/olist]

